        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">This dataset includes a method of producing a cathode for a lithium ion battery. Spinell type lithium manganese oxide acts as a Li+-ion accumulator. Free Li+-ions move out of the spinell type LiMn2O4 (charge) to the electrolyte or from the electrolyte back to the LiMn2O4 spinell (discharge).\n\n# Included processes\nThis dataset incudes the production of a cathode for a lithium-ion battery. Active material is lithium manganese oxide, binder is LHB-108P (styrene butadiene) with the solvent water. Collector foil is aluminium, pretreated with NaOH. The collector foil is coated on 1 side with the slurry (active material, binder, solvent and conductive carbon). Then, the coated foil is dried in a "dry channel" and then coiled up. The same procedure is done for the second side of the collector foil.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
